# Versioning and releases

One semver for the whole product. Root `package.json` is the source of truth. Copy it to `src.create`, `src.player`, and `src.app` with `node scripts/sync-versions.js`. Do not version create / player / app independently.

- Stay on `0.x` until a disc from this tree is the compatibility promise; then `1.0.0`.
- First release is `0.1.0` (git tag `v0.1.0`).
- Notes live in `releases/<version>.md` — **same text** for the GitHub Release body and Disc Creator Help (f0).
- Help / header show `BeebSID Tools vX.Y.Z`, not three component versions.
- Pages deploys `main`; the tag is the named snapshot.

When cutting a release: write `releases/X.Y.Z.md`, bump root version, run `sync-versions`, commit, then `node scripts/publish-release.js` (`gh release create` + `--notes-file`).
